    "text": "Child allowance - Family Service Skip to main content Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg Child allowance Child allowance General: You are entitled to child allowance as soon as a child is born. Child allowance is paid by the state, it does not depend on your income and is tax-free . Families receive €250 per child . Generally speaking, child allowance is paid until the child turns 18 . Special rules: For children who are still completing vocational training or studying (including in preparation for a doctoral degree), child allowance can be paid until the child turns 25 . For children with a disability, it is irrelevant whether or not they are studying or completing training. Applying for child allowance: After a change of rules introduced in 2023, all staff should apply for child allowance from the family benefits office at the Federal Employment Agency (Familienkasse der Agentur für Arbeit). Application forms are available for downloading . Family benefits office (responsible for Erlangen and Nuremberg): Familienkasse Bayern Nord Solgerstraße 1 90429 Nürnberg Phone: +49 800 4555530 Services Use Tab to navigate through menu items, Enter to select, Escape to close, or use the Close button. Back Close No menu items found. Structure Use Tab to navigate through menu items, Enter to select, Escape to close, or use the Close button. Back Close FAU Faculties Faculty of Humanities, Social Sciences, and Theology Faculty of Humanities, Social Sciences, and Theology Department of Classical World and Asian Cultures Department of English, American and Romance Studies Department of Subject-specific Education Research Department of German and Comparative Studies Department of History Department of Media Studies and Art History Department of Education Department of Psychology Department of Social Sciences and Philosophy School of Theology Department of Islamic Religious Studies Department of Sport Science and Sport Department of Digital Humanities and S